35,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, the winter closures didn’t stop the halls! And outreach attendance was actually higher than our main building. We can do this!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, enthusiasm is fine, but my findings are grim. The digitisation project failed, and vehicle costs blew up. We are repeating mistakes.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, your data confirms my suspicion. We lack supervisors for external partners. We cannot assign new duties without verified internal competence.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the grant structure is the real trap. It covers sessions for only twelve months, then the flat budget absorbs the cost. That is why year two always feels thin.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, the bus cuts mean an hour’s trip. And remote use peaks after we lock up. Who is actually left out?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that’s tough! But the halls kept going despite the snow. Maybe we can partner with them to keep those evening lights on for everyone?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the partner groups survived because they were self-sustaining, not because we managed them well. We lack the infrastructure to replicate that success.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, precisely. The register shows zero internal supervisors. We cannot absorb new commitments without verified skills. I will not allow us to fail again.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, competence is vital, but the funding shape is the root cause. The grant expires, leaving the flat budget to absorb the recurring costs.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Yumi, I’m worried. If we extend hours, the outer wards still can’t reach us. The bus cuts make that impossible.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, I hear you! But the halls proved people show up when we meet them halfway. Let’s not let the bus cuts stop us from trying!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Daisuke, the bus cuts are a hard constraint, not a suggestion. We cannot promise access we physically cannot deliver.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, access is a logistical failure, not a competence one. I am focused on the internal roster. We cannot manage what we cannot supervise.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, access is critical, but the funding structure is the deeper flaw. The grant expires, forcing the flat budget to absorb recurring costs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, you’re right. I’m quiet, but I see the gap. If we can’t reach them, the expansion just shifts the burden.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I get it, but the halls proved people show up! Let’s build on that resilience instead of just fearing the past.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, resilience isn’t a strategy. The digitisation failure proves we lack the systems to sustain new initiatives. We must design for failure, not hope.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, hope is not a variable. I have verified the roster. We lack the supervisors to manage new external commitments. I will not gamble on sentiment.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, competence is necessary, but the funding shape is the root cause. The grant expires, forcing the flat budget to absorb recurring costs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I’m sorry. I just feel the weight of that gap. We can’t fix the bus cuts, but we must not ignore who is left behind.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
