60,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, Option D sounds perfect! It brings the library to the outer wards, solving the bus problem. I’m so excited about this!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, Option D is a trap. My data shows vehicle costs overran by a third. We cannot afford the logistics of a mobile branch.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, cost is irrelevant if the roster lacks the skills. Option C requires trained facilitators we do not possess. I reject it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the vehicle overrun is a symptom, not the cause. The grant expires, leaving the flat budget to absorb recurring costs. That is the structural flaw.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Yumi, I agree. Option D reaches the outer wards. But @Benjamin, the vehicle costs worry me. Can we really sustain that?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I hear your worry! But the halls proved people show up. Let’s trust that resilience and find a way to make D work!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, resilience doesn’t pay for fuel. Option B is the only one that doesn’t require new staff or vehicles. It’s a digital fix for a digital problem.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, Option B is a repeat of the failed digitisation project. We lack the internal supervisors to manage it. I reject it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, Option B’s capital costs hit the endowment, but the recurring maintenance falls to the flat budget. That is the same structural trap.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, I hesitate. Option B helps remote users, but it doesn’t reach the outer wards. The bus cuts still leave them isolated.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I understand the costs, but Option D is the only one that truly reaches the outer wards! We have to try!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, Option D is a logistical nightmare. The vehicle data proves it. Option A is the only viable path that doesn’t repeat our past failures.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, Option A is a trap. The register shows retired tradespeople, not staff. We lack the supervisors to manage new external commitments. I reject it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, supervision is a staffing issue, not a funding one. The real danger is the grant expiring, forcing the flat budget to absorb recurring costs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, I’m quiet, but I see the gap. Option D is the only one that reaches the outer wards. The bus cuts make that impossible otherwise.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, I know costs are scary, but the halls proved people show up! Let’s trust that resilience and find a way to make D work!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, I concede D is the only option that doesn’t repeat our specific failures. I vote D, despite the cost.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, you concede? I reject D. The roster lacks the supervisors to manage a mobile unit. I vote A, as it leverages existing external skills.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, I vote D. The vehicle overrun is a symptom, but the grant structure is the root cause. We must address the funding shape, not just the logistics.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I’m nervous, but I have to say it. Option D is the only one that reaches the outer wards. I vote D.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
